  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of new and revised country sector policies (hunting, energy, agriculture, waste management, and tourism) incorporating MSB issues i) submitted as recommendations to and ii)approved  by national governments in the project countries</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2016">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">22 new policies submitted of which 13 in progress and 9 approved;
Egypt: 1 in progress and 3 approved
Jordan: 2 in progress and 2 approved
Lebanon: 5 in progress and 3 approved
Regional : 4 in progress and 1 approved</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">start scoping analysis of current situation and gaps for a MSB Flyway Monitoring Program

Continue transfer into the new platform of the Sensitivity Tool 2. Data update and expansion including collection of new data and revising species status based on new Red List results 3. Promotion of the sensitivity tool 

Hold Project Board meeting in the 2nd half of Feb. 2020. Possible second meeting to be defined. 

Midterm Evaluation prepare TOR and hire a consultant</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Current situation analysis and gaps for MSBII flyway monitoring programme

Data update and promote sensitivity tools.

MTR consultant was hired and drafted the MTR report.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">National vehicles on the five sectors delivering positive results in Djibouti, Jordan, Ethiopia, Sudan, Jordan, and Lebanon delivering positive results. Strengthen collaboration with Intergovernmental Task Force on Illegal Killing, Taking and Trade of Migratory Birds in the Mediterranean (MIKT) task force. Special focus on sector related CMS Energy Task Force ETF. Raise awareness of the flyway and altered social and cultural behaviours through sector-events. Implement MTR Recommendations</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Launching a national bird monitoring data base in Jordan. MoU on mainstreaming bird conservation considerations in the wind farm project in Djibouti signed. New energy support contracts in Lebanon, Jordan and Ethiopia. A Road Map to tackle illegal bird killing in the Middle East was drafted. Two Working Groups (Technical WG &#x2013; Powerlines WG) were established under ETF with BirdLife membership. Regional tourism, IKB and energy webinars successfully delivered. The number of green jobs being generated directly or indirectly by the project and a new CMS related indicator are suggested to be incorporated within PRF. Start planning the &#x201c;new phase&#x201d; of the project.</narrative>
